{"book":19,"chapter":10,"rubric":"LINUX NETWORKING / CHAPTER 10","slides":[{"title":"A bridge is a switch in the kernel","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"Bridge","main":"A layer-2 software switch: ports, MAC addresses, an interface of its own.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Kernel","Ports","br0","Layer 2"],"captions":["A bridge is a software switch inside the kernel","A port: a NIC, one end of a veth, or a VM's tap","The bridge itself shows up as interface br0 and holds the host address","It decides by destination MAC and knows nothing of IP"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"software switch in the kernel","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"software switch in the kernel","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ports: eth, veth, tap","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"software switch in the kernel","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ports: eth, veth, tap","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"br0: interface and host address","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"software switch in the kernel","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ports: eth, veth, tap","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"br0: interface and host address","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"decides by MAC, not by IP","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.1,16.3,28.4]}]},{"title":"Create a bridge and add a port","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"Commands","main":"ip link add type bridge, set master, nomaster; the address goes on the bridge.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Create","Port","Check","Remove"],"captions":["Add a device of type bridge and bring it up","set master makes eth1 a port, the host address goes on br0","bridge link show lists the ports and their states","nomaster takes the interface out; brctl is obsolete"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add name br0 type bridge","$ ip link set br0 up","$ ip link set eth1 master br0","$ ip addr add 192.168.1.10/24 dev br0","$ bridge link show","3: eth1: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ ip link set eth1 nomaster"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add name br0 type bridge","$ ip link set br0 up","$ ip link set eth1 master br0","$ ip addr add 192.168.1.10/24 dev br0","$ bridge link show","3: eth1: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ ip link set eth1 nomaster"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add name br0 type bridge","$ ip link set br0 up","$ ip link set eth1 master br0","$ ip addr add 192.168.1.10/24 dev br0","$ bridge link show","3: eth1: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ ip link set eth1 nomaster"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add name br0 type bridge","$ ip link set br0 up","$ ip link set eth1 master br0","$ ip addr add 192.168.1.10/24 dev br0","$ bridge link show","3: eth1: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ ip link set eth1 nomaster"],"hl":[6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.5,19.9,29.6]}]},{"title":"veth, a virtual cable","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"veth","main":"A pair of devices: a frame into one end comes out of the other.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Pair","Ends","List","Peer"],"captions":["The device is created only as a pair, we name both ends","Both ends are brought up; one is attached to a bridge (or a netns)","The interface list shows veth0@veth1 and veth1@veth0","ethtool -S shows peer_ifindex, which leads to the far end"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add veth0 type veth peer name veth1","$ ip link set veth0 up","$ ip link set veth1 master br0 up","$ ip -br link show type veth","veth0@veth1  UP  5a:8c:d4:1e:11:90","veth1@veth0  UP  8e:3c:01:7a:22:b4","$ ethtool -S veth0","  peer_ifindex: 8"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add veth0 type veth peer name veth1","$ ip link set veth0 up","$ ip link set veth1 master br0 up","$ ip -br link show type veth","veth0@veth1  UP  5a:8c:d4:1e:11:90","veth1@veth0  UP  8e:3c:01:7a:22:b4","$ ethtool -S veth0","  peer_ifindex: 8"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add veth0 type veth peer name veth1","$ ip link set veth0 up","$ ip link set veth1 master br0 up","$ ip -br link show type veth","veth0@veth1  UP  5a:8c:d4:1e:11:90","veth1@veth0  UP  8e:3c:01:7a:22:b4","$ ethtool -S veth0","  peer_ifindex: 8"],"hl":[3,4,5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add veth0 type veth peer name veth1","$ ip link set veth0 up","$ ip link set veth1 master br0 up","$ ip -br link show type veth","veth0@veth1  UP  5a:8c:d4:1e:11:90","veth1@veth0  UP  8e:3c:01:7a:22:b4","$ ethtool -S veth0","  peer_ifindex: 8"],"hl":[6,7],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.7,19.1,27.2]}]},{"title":"Reading ip -d link","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"ip -d","main":"Times in hundredths of a second, STP, VLAN filtering, bridge_id.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Timers","STP and VLAN","bridge_id","Port"],"captions":["Times in hundredths of a second: ageing_time 30000 is 300 s","stp_state 0: STP is off; priority 32768; vlan_filtering 0","bridge_id: priority and MAC (by default the lowest port MAC)","A port: bridge_slave, state, priority 32, cost, learning, flood"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip -d link show br0","bridge forward_delay 1500 hello_time 200","  max_age 2000 ageing_time 30000","  stp_state 0 priority 32768","  vlan_filtering 0 vlan_protocol 802.1Q","  bridge_id 8000.525400aabbcc","$ ip -d link show veth1","bridge_slave state forwarding priority 32","  cost 2 hairpin off learning on flood on"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip -d link show br0","bridge forward_delay 1500 hello_time 200","  max_age 2000 ageing_time 30000","  stp_state 0 priority 32768","  vlan_filtering 0 vlan_protocol 802.1Q","  bridge_id 8000.525400aabbcc","$ ip -d link show veth1","bridge_slave state forwarding priority 32","  cost 2 hairpin off learning on flood on"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip -d link show br0","bridge forward_delay 1500 hello_time 200","  max_age 2000 ageing_time 30000","  stp_state 0 priority 32768","  vlan_filtering 0 vlan_protocol 802.1Q","  bridge_id 8000.525400aabbcc","$ ip -d link show veth1","bridge_slave state forwarding priority 32","  cost 2 hairpin off learning on flood on"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip -d link show br0","bridge forward_delay 1500 hello_time 200","  max_age 2000 ageing_time 30000","  stp_state 0 priority 32768","  vlan_filtering 0 vlan_protocol 802.1Q","  bridge_id 8000.525400aabbcc","$ ip -d link show veth1","bridge_slave state forwarding priority 32","  cost 2 hairpin off learning on flood on"],"hl":[6,7,8],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.6,18.8,28.6]}]},{"title":"The forwarding table, FDB","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"FDB","main":"The bridge remembers the sender per port; dynamic entries age out.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Table","Dynamic","permanent","Ageing"],"captions":["bridge fdb show: MAC, port, bridge (the sender of every frame is remembered)","No word at the end: a dynamic entry, learned from frames","permanent: the ports' own addresses, they never age","Dynamic entries age out after 300 s without frames from the source"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge fdb show br br0","fe:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0 permanent","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","52:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0","fe:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0 permanent"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge fdb show br br0","fe:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0 permanent","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","52:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0","fe:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0 permanent"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge fdb show br br0","fe:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0 permanent","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","52:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0","fe:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0 permanent"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge fdb show br br0","fe:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0 permanent","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","52:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0","fe:54:00:44:55:66 dev vnet1 master br0 permanent"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[11.5,20.0,27.7]}]},{"title":"STP and port states","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"STP","main":"STP is off by default; once on, it walks a port through four steps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["blocking","listening","learning","forwarding"],"captions":["blocking: the port processes only BPDUs","listening: 15 s, data frames are dropped","learning: another 15 s, it learns addresses but does not forward","forwarding: the port works fully; without STP ports start here"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"blocking","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"blocking","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"listening\n15 s","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"blocking","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"listening\n15 s","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":224.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"learning\n15 s","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":174.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":185.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"blocking","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"listening\n15 s","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":224.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"learning\n15 s","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":174.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":185.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":313.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"forwarding","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a3","x1":263.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":274.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[7.7,15.7,28.4]}]},{"title":"An 802.1Q VLAN subinterface","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"eth0.100","main":"ip link add link eth0 type vlan id 100: a tagged port of the host.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Create","Name","Details","MTU"],"captions":["link is the parent, type vlan and id (1-4094) make a tagged port","The name eth0.100 is only a convention, the id sets the number","ip -d link: protocol 802.1Q and id 100","MTU equals the parent's and never exceeds it; on the wire the frame is 4 bytes longer"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add link eth0 name eth0.100","    type vlan id 100","$ ip link set eth0.100 up","$ ip -d link show eth0.100","5: eth0.100@eth0: <...> mtu 1500 ...","    vlan protocol 802.1Q id 100 <REORDER_HDR>"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add link eth0 name eth0.100","    type vlan id 100","$ ip link set eth0.100 up","$ ip -d link show eth0.100","5: eth0.100@eth0: <...> mtu 1500 ...","    vlan protocol 802.1Q id 100 <REORDER_HDR>"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add link eth0 name eth0.100","    type vlan id 100","$ ip link set eth0.100 up","$ ip -d link show eth0.100","5: eth0.100@eth0: <...> mtu 1500 ...","    vlan protocol 802.1Q id 100 <REORDER_HDR>"],"hl":[3,5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link add link eth0 name eth0.100","    type vlan id 100","$ ip link set eth0.100 up","$ ip -d link show eth0.100","5: eth0.100@eth0: <...> mtu 1500 ...","    vlan protocol 802.1Q id 100 <REORDER_HDR>"],"hl":[4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.5,18.7,24.4]}]},{"title":"A VLAN-aware bridge","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"vlan_filtering","main":"PVID, untagged and a VLAN list on every port; one bridge for all VLANs.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Enable","pvid","Trunk","Table"],"captions":["vlan_filtering 1 turns filtering on, without it tags are ignored","pvid: where untagged frames go; untagged: the tag is removed on egress","Port eth0 is a tagged trunk with VLAN 20 (and 1 by default)","bridge vlan show: each entry has the PVID and Egress Untagged flags"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link set br0 type bridge vlan_filtering 1","$ bridge vlan add dev veth1 vid 20 pvid untagged","$ bridge vlan add dev eth0 vid 20","$ bridge vlan show","port   vlan-id","eth0   1 PVID Egress Untagged","       20","veth1  1 Egress Untagged","       20 PVID Egress Untagged"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link set br0 type bridge vlan_filtering 1","$ bridge vlan add dev veth1 vid 20 pvid untagged","$ bridge vlan add dev eth0 vid 20","$ bridge vlan show","port   vlan-id","eth0   1 PVID Egress Untagged","       20","veth1  1 Egress Untagged","       20 PVID Egress Untagged"],"hl":[1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link set br0 type bridge vlan_filtering 1","$ bridge vlan add dev veth1 vid 20 pvid untagged","$ bridge vlan add dev eth0 vid 20","$ bridge vlan show","port   vlan-id","eth0   1 PVID Egress Untagged","       20","veth1  1 Egress Untagged","       20 PVID Egress Untagged"],"hl":[2,5,6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ip link set br0 type bridge vlan_filtering 1","$ bridge vlan add dev veth1 vid 20 pvid untagged","$ bridge vlan add dev eth0 vid 20","$ bridge vlan show","port   vlan-id","eth0   1 PVID Egress Untagged","       20","veth1  1 Egress Untagged","       20 PVID Egress Untagged"],"hl":[3,4,5,6,7,8],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.2,19.3,27.7]}]},{"title":"Bridges in KVM and oVirt","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"KVM, oVirt","main":"A machine's tap is a bridge port: virbr0 for NAT, br0 for the LAN.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["tap","virbr0","br0","oVirt"],"captions":["libvirt creates the VM's tap (usually vnet0, vnet1) and makes it a bridge port","The default network: bridge virbr0, host address 192.168.122.1","Your own network: bridge br0 with the physical NIC, address on the bridge","oVirt (classic layout): a bridge per logical network, over bond0.50 for a VLAN"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"tap vnet0 -> bridge port","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"tap vnet0 -> bridge port","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"virbr0: NAT, 192.168.122.1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"tap vnet0 -> bridge port","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"virbr0: NAT, 192.168.122.1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"br0 + eth0: VM on the LAN","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"tap vnet0 -> bridge port","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"virbr0: NAT, 192.168.122.1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"br0 + eth0: VM on the LAN","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"oVirt: bridge over bond0.50","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.0,18.0,27.4]}]},{"title":"No network in a VM: a checklist","sub":"Chapter 10 · Linux networking","short":"Diagnosis","main":"Port and state, VLAN and PVID, an FDB entry, counters.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Port","VLAN","FDB","Counters"],"captions":["Is the port in the right bridge, in the forwarding state?","Is the VLAN there, does the PVID match, is untagged set?","Is the guest MAC learned on this port?","Do the port counters grow? iptables sees a bridge only with br_netfilter"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge link show master br0","12: vnet0: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ bridge vlan show dev vnet0","vnet0  20 PVID Egress Untagged","$ bridge fdb show br br0 | grep 52:54:00","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","$ ip -s link show vnet0","RX: bytes packets errors dropped ..."],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge link show master br0","12: vnet0: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ bridge vlan show dev vnet0","vnet0  20 PVID Egress Untagged","$ bridge fdb show br br0 | grep 52:54:00","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","$ ip -s link show vnet0","RX: bytes packets errors dropped ..."],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge link show master br0","12: vnet0: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ bridge vlan show dev vnet0","vnet0  20 PVID Egress Untagged","$ bridge fdb show br br0 | grep 52:54:00","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","$ ip -s link show vnet0","RX: bytes packets errors dropped ..."],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ bridge link show master br0","12: vnet0: <...> master br0 state forwarding","$ bridge vlan show dev vnet0","vnet0  20 PVID Egress Untagged","$ bridge fdb show br br0 | grep 52:54:00","52:54:00:11:22:33 dev vnet0 master br0","$ ip -s link show vnet0","RX: bytes packets errors dropped ..."],"hl":[6,7],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[10.1,20.0,26.7]}]}]}